1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:12,522
The Novak kitchen is sold. Hand it to the shop floor from the job's Output tab.

2
00:00:12,522 --> 00:00:15,700
First, the export check: read it before anything is cut.

3
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:20,782
Placeholder tools and machine data: load the real N-200 values before running programs.

4
00:00:20,782 --> 00:00:26,296
Small parts like the 2" x 6" corner cleat get a vacuum warning: hold them down or cut by hand.

5
00:00:26,296 --> 00:00:29,150
Machine output switches stay off. The floor needs the paperwork.

6
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:36,921
Sheet maps PDF: one page per sheet, every part numbered where it sits.

7
00:00:36,921 --> 00:00:44,585
The operator lays each map next to its sheet and checks the parts as they come off.

8
00:00:44,585 --> 00:00:52,378
Labels PDF: a sheet header label, then one label per part in cut order.

9
00:00:52,378 --> 00:00:59,698
Each label carries the job, cabinet, part, size, banded edges and a barcode.

10
00:00:59,698 --> 00:01:04,168
Labels ZPL sends the same labels straight to a Zebra printer at the machine.

11
00:01:04,168 --> 00:01:19,917
Cut list CSV for anything cut on the panel saw, and for the edgebander operator.

12
00:01:19,917 --> 00:01:24,533
BOM CSV goes to purchasing: hinges, plates, slides and edgeband to have on hand.

13
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:29,635
Maps, labels, cut list and order list: the job is ready for the floor.
